        "identifier": "PALOMAR-2026-10-17-000004 (jtraverso/pseudorandom-hypergraph-matchings @ 3957f3c)",
        "note": "The Ehard-Glock-Joos formalization (Pseudorandom hypergraph matchings). GJKKL/Vendor/Freedman.lean is its PseudorandomLib/Freedman.lean at commit 3957f3c0dbc34fd310cb5fecf7941fddc9ef6c8f with one import changed, and the hypergraph vocabulary used in the statement (Pseudorandom.IsUniform, degree, codegree, IsMatching) is its PseudorandomLib/Defs.lean, byte for byte, through the CDR III corpus copy below.",
        "relationship": "builds-on"
      },
      {
        "identifier": "https://github.com/jtraverso/cdr-steiner-preprints/releases/tag/paper-iii-v1.0",
        "note": "Lean sources of CDR III (Prescribed block types and abundance in bicolored Steiner triple systems, preprint 1.0, DOI 10.5281/zenodo.24201563; archive CDRIII_Lean_v1.0.zip, SHA-256 08dcee5b5d67d00d1f561988e8c716c57c92d250ca54270f3d417429fb52e649). Three of its modules are vendored here without any change, under their original module names: RequestProject.Pseudorandom.Defs (hypergraph vocabulary), FiniteProb (finite product probability) and Bernstein (the one-step Bernstein bound). They coincide with the corresponding PseudorandomLib modules of the Ehard-Glock-Joos formalization up to the module prefix. File hashes are in evidence/PACKAGING.json. The Challenge copies the four vocabulary definitions its statement uses.",
        "relationship": "builds-on"
